			"notes": "# WorldHeightLimit v1.1.0\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- Added Bukkit and Spigot support.\n- Added Folia support across the supported version range.\n- Paper and Purpur remain supported.\n- Release files are now split into clear platform groups:\n  - Paper / Purpur / Folia\n  - Spigot / Bukkit\n\n## Commands\n\n- Added `/worldheightlimit debug`.\n- Added `/worldheightlimit worlds`.\n- The same commands also work through the legacy `/highbuildlimit` alias.\n- `/worldheightlimit` is now the primary command.\n\n## Diagnostics\n\n- `/debug` shows server, plugin, world, height, datapack, dimension, and restriction information.\n- `/worlds` lists all loaded worlds with their active height ranges.\n- Status output now includes the generated technical world height.\n\n## Packaging\n\n- JAR files now use platform/version-specific names for easier publishing and downloading.\n- Internal class/package names now match the `WorldHeightLimit` branding.\n\n## Compatibility Notes\n\n- Existing `highbuildlimit.*` permission nodes are unchanged.\n- Existing `/highbuildlimit` commands still work as aliases.\n- Existing configs remain compatible."
		}
